-ounce bags; and regular Cheetos Jumbo Puffs at 49.94 dollars for twelve title-declared 2.38-ounce bags. Generic Item Weight, Package Dimensions or Product Dimensions fields differ from or ambiguously repeat some title quantities. Complete current ingredient, nutrition, allergen and serving panels are absent. Background sources discuss clean-label and natural-label ambiguity, MSG identity and umami function, broader glutamate flavoring, additive and colorant functions, and natural-versus-artificial flavor source classes. Four community pages contain only scoped debates about naturally occurring MSG, contested MSG beliefs, front-label interpretation and a small self-reported child-snack survey. No source supplies an exact current formula comparison, ingredient amounts, exposure, child-specific outcome, matched same-product clean-label control, delivered-price verification or blinded family acceptability result.","target":"Audit what every frozen seller, concept and community source can and cannot establish about clean-label snack claims and price. Build an exact-offer table with literal SKU, variant, pack, mass, price, claim and unknown fields; retain quantity ambiguities; show conditional price-per-declared-mass arithmetic; and state why the five offers are not a matched premium experiment. Explain clean-label and natural-label ambiguity, the difference between monosodium glutamate and broader glutamate flavoring, and the functional or source-class limits of additive, color and flavor terminology without making health, safety, exposure or medical claims. Treat the community debates and child-snack survey only as scoped belief and method evidence. Then specify the exact current label, formula, allergen, quantity and delivered-cost checks and the smallest practical comparable repeated family trial with marketing masked, portions randomized, acceptability and waste recorded, and predeclared stops. End with a lowest-cost passing, keep-baseline, smaller-matched-trial or 